# Line endings are LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Two things depend on this. rustfmt.toml sets newline_style = "Unix", so a
# CRLF checkout makes `cargo fmt --check` report every file as unformatted —
# which is exactly what the first Windows CI leg did. And the git fixture is
# built by copying files from fixtures/content byte for byte, so a CRLF checkout
# would change every committed blob and therefore every fixture commit SHA,
# breaking the determinism the fixture exists to provide.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
